# Python environment
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw training audio + every trained-model/experiment artifact this project produces.
# These were previously tracked (1006 files, ~1.85GB across belt/brake/sway +
# processed_data/ alone, plus ablation_results/ and aug_technique_diagnostic/'s own
# copies of trained models from earlier experiments) in this repo's git history --
# regenerable from the raw audio via preprocessing.py + the train_*.py scripts, and
# not meant to be pushed to a public remote. Untracked going forward (see the commit
# that added this comment); the data still exists in past commits until the history
# itself is rewritten -- that's a separate, deliberate decision, not done here.
belt/
brake/
sway/
processed_data/
processed_data_backup_*/
ablation_results/
aug_technique_diagnostic/

# Large regenerable feature-cache arrays (rebuilt by preprocessing.py / run_augmentation_ablation.py)
X_train_mel.npy
X_val_mel.npy
X_test_mel.npy
X_train_mfcc.npy
X_val_mfcc.npy
X_test_mfcc.npy
features.csv

# sounds_curation/: caches + downloaded candidates from the concluded Freesound
# investigation (see SESSION_HANDOFF.md section 3) -- regenerable via
# freesound_downloader.py + score_candidates.py, not part of the deployed pipeline.
sounds_curation/candidates/
sounds_curation/*_cache.pkl
sounds_curation/manifest.json

# BEATs checkpoint (~344MB, downloaded automatically by train_beats.py on first run from
# the HF mirror -- see its module docstring). Vendored source files (BEATs.py/backbone.py/
# modules.py) ARE tracked, just not this binary weights file.
beats_vendor/*.pt

# EfficientAT checkpoint (~19MB, downloaded automatically via torch.hub by
# train_efficientat_finetune.py on first run -- model_dir="resources" is set inside the
# vendored models/mn/model.py itself, relative to wherever the script is run from).
resources/

# OS/editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local Claude Code tooling state (machine-specific, not project source)
.claude/
